le.","signature":"On first entry to weekly utilization, each bar fill settles from scaleX(1.04) to scaleX(1) over 600ms cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), staggered 40ms, while measured labels stay fixed."},"projectId":"69693301273542272","prompts":{"S-1":"Design the sign-in page alone, without an employee or administrator shell. Use a quiet, light page with a compact Folio3 Parking wordmark and a centered, modest sign-in panel; no oversized hero. The first thing the eye meets is the heading “Sign in to Folio3 Parking,” followed by one sentence explaining that employees use their Folio3 Google account. Show one primary button, “Continue with Google,” with a recognizable Google sign-in mark, and a small privacy reassurance that parking details appear only after the account is verified as an active Folio3 employee. Successful OAuth callback handling must only establish a session after Google token signature, issuer, and audience validation, OAuth state verification, and active employee confirmation; do not draw a callback page. Keep the surrounding canvas intentionally open. The page must reflow cleanly for phone, tablet, and desktop, with a touch-sized button.\nThe product's sample data, the same on every page; where this page shows any of it, use it exactly: Product and timezone: Folio3 Parking for the Bengaluru office; all displayed dates and times use Asia/Kolkata (IST, UTC+05:30), the product’s one office timezone. Current sample moment: Tue 19 May 2026, 9:15 AM IST. Daily release time: 9:00 AM IST. Work calendar: Monday–Friday. Parking capacity: P1 has 40 spaces, P2 has 30 spaces, total 70. Current claimable count is 2: P1-18 released today by Devika Iyer and P2-14 released today by Maya Krishnan. Ananya Rao’s P1-12 is still Reserved today. Employees and records: Ananya Rao — Product Design, Employee; dedicated P1-12; registered vehicle KA03MN4821. Rohan Mehta — Engineering, Employee; no dedicated space; registered vehicle KA05PQ7712. Priya Nair — People Operations, Parking Administrator; dedicated P2-08; registered vehicle KA01AB2345. Devika Iyer — Finance, Employee; dedicated P1-18; registered vehicle KA04CD6190. Maya Krishnan — Engineering, Employee; dedicated P2-14; registered vehicle KA03GH8820. Kabir Shah — Security, Security Guard; no dedicated space; no registered vehicle. Jonah Lee — IT Support, Employee; no dedicated space; no registered vehicle. Ananya has scheduled releases for Thu 21 May and Mon 25 May 2026. Weekly report sample: reporting week Mon 11 May–Sun 17 May 2026, generated Mon 18 May at 8:00 AM IST; 350 eligible allocations, 286 used, 81.7% utilization (100 × 286 / 350); daily used/eligible counts Mon 58/70, Tue 57/70, Wed 56/70, Thu 58/70, Fri 57/70; 12 releases, 10 claims, 8 unused dedicated allocations and 4 unused temporary allocations. Named report recipients: Priya Nair (priya.nair@folio3.com, Parking Administrator) and Jonah Lee (jonah.lee@folio3.com, Employee); only the administrator recipient receives employee-identifying weekly report email. Use each person’s own distinct, consistent real-photo identity anywhere portraits appear; do not reuse one person’s face for another. These figures, names, roles, floor labels, plates, dates and statuses remain identical across all screens.","S-10":"The shared header reads “Folio3 Parking”; the menu sits beside the brand and contains “Overview,” “Employees,” “Parking setup,” “Weekly report,” “Entry checks,” and “Audit history,” in that order. On the right, a profile menu shows “Priya Nair” and “Parking Administrator.” Design one administrator setup page with compact, clearly separated sections in this order: daily release time, floor capacity, work calendar, named weekly report recipients, and role assignments. Show the current daily release time as 9:00 AM in the single office timezone Asia/Kolkata (IST); floor counts as P1 40 and P2 30, total 70; and the working calendar as Monday–Friday. In report recipients, show Priya Nair (priya.nair@folio3.com, Parkin